     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>A path that visits each vertex exactly once is a Hamilton path. Recall that a path is a walk that has no repeated vertices or edges. It does not need to start and end on the same vertex.</p>\n<p>This sequence is not a Hamilton path since vertex <i>b</i> is visited in the midst of the path, as well as being the start and ending vertex.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "No"
